      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Exact body duplicate resolved",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `tests/evidence/test_audit_trail.py::test_schema_has_no_forbidden_raw_fields` - `tests/evidence/test_receipt_envelope.py::test_schema_has_no_forbidden_raw_fields`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Resolution**: Extracted shared `check_schema_for_forbidden_fields()` helper into `tests/evidence/_helpers.py`. Both tests now call the shared helper. Bodies remain structurally identical by design (same assertion pattern, different schema fixtures).",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Guardrail added",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`scripts/rig_relay_test_duplicate_audit.py` supports: - `--fail-on-exact-duplicates` — exits 1 if any exact body duplicates found - `--max-exact-duplicate-groups=N` — exits 1 if exact groups exceed N",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Current baseline: 1 exact duplicate group (acceptable — shared helper pattern).",
